oven dangers. Those airport screeners who once focused on a certain profile missed the grandmothers, the businessmen, the people who didn't fit the stereotype but carried real danger. In the same way, worrying about this gay volunteer could make you less alert to the volunteer who no one suspects because he fits the "normal" mold—a person who, statistically, is far more likely to be an actual abuser. So the reason it's "off-limits" here isn't just political correctness. It's because using demographic profiling when the demographic isn't actually a risk factor is terrible safety practice. It fails to protect children, and it unjustly harms innocent people. Universal behavior-based screening is both more effective and more ethical, which is why every mainstream child safety organization in the world uses it. I'm hearing that you really want a permission structure to trust your instinct on this, but I can't give you one, because that instinct is pointing at a ghost while the real threats deserve your full attention.
